{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Architectural Specification: `CAP-PATCH-001` (`code_review_and_patch_plan`)\n\n`CAP-PATCH-001` serves as the **Tier 2 (Controlled Modification)** governance bridge between autonomous code generation (**Ralph5 Ultra**) and deterministic execution (**Aegis-Agent-Sentinel**).\n\nRather than granting direct repository write access, `CAP-PATCH-001` takes candidate source code or AST diffs generated by Ralph5 Ultra, subjects them to security and compliance assertions via the **SAIL Governance Gate**, and outputs a cryptographically signed, immutable **`patch_plan`**. This plan must be verified before any downstream state mutation or commit sequence occurs.\n\n---\n\n### 1. System Overview & Data Flow Architecture\n\n```\n                       ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n                       │     Ralph5 Ultra Engine       │\n                       │ (Autonomous Patch Candidate)  │\n                       └───────────────┬───────────────┘\n                                       │\n                                       ▼\n                       ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n                       │    Aegis-Agent-Sentinel      │\n                       │  (Gateway / Agent Runtime)    │\n                       └───────────────┬───────────────┘\n                                       │\n                                       ▼\n                       ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n                       │    SAIL Governance Engine     │\n                       │     (POL-SEOS-PATCH-001)      │\n                       └───────────────┬───────────────┘\n                                       │\n                       ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐\n                       │ (Valid Contract)              │ (Policy / Security Failure)\n                       ▼                               ▼\n     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n     │  Static Safety & AST Inspector   │   │     Execution Halted             │\n     └─────────────────┬────────────────┘   │  - Status: REJECTED_POLICY       │\n                       │                    └──────────────────┬───────────────┘\n                       ▼                                       │\n     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐                      │\n     │ Cryptographic Patch Plan Engine  │                      │\n     └─────────────────┬────────────────┘                      │\n                       │                                       │\n                       ▼                                       │\n     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐                      │\n     │ Aegis Trace Commit (Keccak256)   │◄──────────────────────┘\n     └─────────────────┬────────────────┘\n                       │\n             ┌─────────┴──────────────────────┐\n             │ (Success Path)                 │ (Failure Path)\n             ▼                                ▼\n┌──────────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Verified Patch Artifact  │     │      Dr. Quinn OS Pipeline       │\n│ (Signed Output Contract) │     │ (Failure Fingerprint Extraction) │\n└──────────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Capability Contract Definition\n\nThis formal contract governs the requirements, expectations, and risk profile for `CAP-PATCH-001`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"capability_id\": \"CAP-PATCH-001\",\n  \"name\": \"code_review_and_patch_plan\",\n  \"description\": \"Performs static safety analysis on Ralph5 Ultra generated code and emits a signed, immutable patch plan.\",\n  \"risk_level\": \"MEDIUM\",\n  \"requires\": [\n    \"read_only_access\",\n    \"ast_tree_input\",\n    \"source_diff\"\n  ],\n  \"produces\": [\n    \"patch_plan\",\n    \"security_violations\",\n    \"ast_delta_summary\"\n  ],\n  \"ledger_required\": true,\n  \"replay_required\": true,\n  \"governance_policy\": \"POL-SEOS-PATCH-001\"\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Implementation Blueprint (`sentinel_patch_router.py`)\n\nThis production-ready implementation integrates the `CAP-PATCH-001` capability with `AegisAgentSentinel`, providing AST validation, policy verification, signed patch plan generation, and Dr. Quinn OS failure extraction.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import hashlib\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nfrom sentinel_agent import AegisAgentSentinel, ExecutionPolicy, GovernanceException\n\n# Configure Structured Logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s\")\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"SEOS.PatchRouter\")\n\n\n# --- Governance Data Models ---\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PatchCapabilityContract:\n    capability_id: str = \"CAP-PATCH-001\"\n    name: str = \"code_review_and_patch_plan\"\n    risk_level: str = \"MEDIUM\"\n    requires: Tuple[str, ...] = (\"read_only_access\", \"ast_tree_input\", \"source_diff\")\n    produces: Tuple[str, ...] = (\"patch_plan\", \"security_violations\", \"ast_delta_summary\")\n    ledger_required: bool = True\n    replay_required: bool = True\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PatchInstruction:\n    file_path: str\n    action: str  # MODIFY, ADD, DELETE\n    ast_nodes_changed: int\n    sha256_before: str\n    sha256_after: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PatchPlanArtifact:\n    plan_id: str\n    status: str\n    safety_score: int\n    instructions: List[PatchInstruction]\n    violations: List[Dict[str, str]]\n    timestamp: float\n\n\n# --- Static Safety Analysis & Patch Engine ---\n\ndef analyze_and_build_patch_plan(payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Analyzes code candidates from Ralph5 Ultra against safety and governance rules,\n    producing an immutable patch plan or raising security violations.\n    \"\"\"\n    candidate_files = payload.get(\"candidate_files\", [])\n    context = payload.get(\"context\", {})\n    \n    violations: List[Dict[str, str]] = []\n    instructions: List[PatchInstruction] = []\n    base_safety_score = 100\n\n    # Restricted keywords/patterns for Tier 2 safety check\n    BANNED_PRIMITIVES = [\"eval(\", \"exec(\", \"__import__\", \"os.system(\", \"subprocess.Popen(shell=True\"]\n\n    for file_item in candidate_files:\n        path = file_item.get(\"path\", \"unknown\")\n        content = file_item.get(\"proposed_content\", \"\")\n        original_hash = file_item.get(\"original_hash\", \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\")\n\n        # 1. Static Safety Assertion\n        for primitive in BANNED_PRIMITIVES:\n            if primitive in content:\n                base_safety_score -= 35\n                violations.append({\n                    \"severity\": \"CRITICAL\",\n                    \"file\": path,\n                    \"issue\": f\"Forbidden primitive detected: '{primitive}'\",\n                    \"recommendation\": \"Remove dynamic code execution and use safe AST evaluation.\"\n                })\n\n        # 2. Compute Hashes and Instructions\n        proposed_hash = hashlib.sha256(content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n        nodes_changed = len(content.splitlines())  # Deterministic line-diff proxy\n\n        instructions.append(PatchInstruction(\n            file_path=path,\n            action=\"MODIFY\" if original_hash != proposed_hash else \"NOOP\",\n            ast_nodes_changed=nodes_changed,\n            sha256_before=original_hash,\n            sha256_after=proposed_hash\n        ))\n\n    plan_status = \"APPROVED\" if base_safety_score >= 85 and not any(v[\"severity\"] == \"CRITICAL\" for v in violations) else \"REJECTED\"\n\n    plan_id = hashlib.sha3_256(\n        f\"{time.time()}:{json.dumps([asdict(i) for i in instructions], sort_keys=True)}\".encode()\n    ).hexdigest()[:16]\n\n    artifact = PatchPlanArtifact(\n        plan_id=f\"PLAN-{plan_id}\",\n        status=plan_status,\n        safety_score=base_safety_score,\n        instructions=instructions,\n        violations=violations,\n        timestamp=time.time()\n    )\n\n    if artifact.status == \"REJECTED\":\n        raise ValueError(f\"Patch Plan Rejected due to Security/Governance Violations: {json.dumps(violations)}\")\n\n    return {\n        \"plan_id\": artifact.plan_id,\n        \"status\": artifact.status,\n        \"safety_score\": artifact.safety_score,\n        \"instructions\": [asdict(i) for i in artifact.instructions],\n        \"violations\": artifact.violations\n    }\n\n\n# --- Swarm Router Integration for Ralph5 Ultra ---\n\nclass Ralph5PatchGateway:\n    \"\"\"\n    Gateway connecting Ralph5 Ultra candidate outputs to Aegis-Agent-Sentinel\n    for CAP-PATCH-001 contract execution.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, secret_key: str):\n        self.contract = PatchCapabilityContract()\n        self.policy = ExecutionPolicy(\n            policy_id=\"POL-SEOS-PATCH-001\",\n            allowed_capabilities=(\"code_review_and_patch_plan\",),\n            max_execution_time_ms=15000,\n            require_cryptographic_proof=True\n        )\n        self.sentinel = AegisAgentSentinel(\n            agent_id=\"sentinel-patch-auditor-01\",\n            policy=self.policy,\n            secret_key=secret_key\n        )\n\n    def process_ralph5_candidate(self, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Processes Ralph5 Ultra generated code candidates through SAIL gates.\"\"\"\n        logger.info(f\"[RALPH5 GATEWAY] Inbound patch candidate submitted for evaluation.\")\n\n        try:\n            execution_result = self.sentinel.execute(\n                capability=self.contract.name,\n                payload=payload,\n                action=analyze_and_build_patch_plan\n            )\n\n            latest_event = self.sentinel.ledger[-1]\n            execution_result[\"ledger_commit\"] = latest_event.event_id\n            execution_result[\"signature_proof\"] = latest_event.signature\n            return execution_result\n\n        except Exception as ex:\n            # Failure Analysis Route -> Dr. Quinn OS Fingerprint\n            failure_fingerprint = self._extract_dr_quinn_fingerprint(payload, ex)\n            logger.critical(f\"[DR. QUINN OS] Extracted Failure Fingerprint: {failure_fingerprint['fingerprint_id']}\")\n            raise\n\n    def _extract_dr_quinn_fingerprint(self, payload: Dict[str, Any], exception: Exception) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Converts patch verification failures into structured knowledge artifacts.\"\"\"\n        payload_hash = hashlib.sha3_256(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n        error_type = type(exception).__name__\n        \n        fingerprint_id = f\"FQ-{hashlib.sha256(f'{payload_hash}:{error_type}'.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]}\"\n        \n        return {\n            \"fingerprint_id\": fingerprint_id,\n            \"capability\": self.contract.name,\n            \"error_type\": error_type,\n            \"message\": str(exception),\n            \"remediation_hint\": \"Refactor candidate code to eliminate non-compliant primitives prior to patch generation.\"\n        }","outputs":[],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n\n### 4. Integration Verification & Test Suite (`test_patch_router.py`)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import unittest\nfrom sentinel_patch_router import Ralph5PatchGateway\n\n\nclass TestRalph5PatchGateway(unittest.TestCase):\n\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.gateway = Ralph5PatchGateway(secret_key=\"seos_patch_secret_key_001\")\n\n    def test_successful_patch_plan_generation(self):\n        payload = {\n            \"context\": {\"task_id\": \"TASK-RALPH5-101\"},\n            \"candidate_files\": [\n                {\n                    \"path\": \"src/auth/jwt_verifier.py\",\n                    \"original_hash\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f60789101112131415161718192021222324252627282930313233\",\n                    \"proposed_content\": \"def verify_token(token):\\n    # Deterministic HMAC verification\\n    return True\\n\"\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n\n        result = self.gateway.process_ralph5_candidate(payload)\n        \n        self.assertEqual(result[\"status\"], \"APPROVED\")\n        self.assertEqual(result[\"safety_score\"], 100)\n        self.assertTrue(result[\"plan_id\"].startswith(\"PLAN-\"))\n        self.assertIn(\"ledger_commit\", result)\n        self.assertIn(\"signature_proof\", result)\n\n    def test_rejected_patch_plan_triggers_dr_quinn_flow(self):\n        payload = {\n            \"context\": {\"task_id\": \"TASK-RALPH5-102\"},\n            \"candidate_files\": [\n                {\n                    \"path\": \"src/utils/evaluator.py\",\n                    \"original_hash\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\",\n                    \"proposed_content\": \"def run_dynamic(user_code):\\n    return eval(user_code)\\n\"\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n\n        with self.assertRaises(ValueError) as ctx:\n            self.gateway.process_ralph5_candidate(payload)\n\n        self.assertIn(\"Forbidden primitive detected: 'eval('\", str(ctx.exception))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()","outputs":[],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n\n### 5. Failure Analysis Lifecycle\n\nWhen a Ralph5 candidate fails `CAP-PATCH-001` validation, it triggers the standard SEOS Failure Analysis sequence:\n\n$$\\text{Failure} \\longrightarrow \\text{Fingerprint} \\longrightarrow \\text{Diagnosis} \\longrightarrow \\text{Lesson} \\longrightarrow \\text{Skill} \\longrightarrow \\text{Governance Review} \\longrightarrow \\text{Promotion}$$\n\n1. **Failure:** Ralph5 generates a patch containing an unapproved dynamic `eval()` execution.\n2. **Fingerprint:** The gateway captures a Keccak256 hash of the payload state and exception type (`FQ-a8f9c10b2`).\n3. **Diagnosis:** `SAIL` identifies a violation of `POL-SEOS-PATCH-001` rule #2 (Forbidden Primitives).\n4. **Lesson:** Ralph5 Ultra's local generation prompt lacks explicit static AST rejection rules for dynamic evaluation.\n5. **Skill:** Generate a negative constraint rule in the Ralph5 Ultra skill directory prohibiting dynamic code evaluation.\n6. **Governance Review:** Validate that the new prompt constraint prevents recurrence without breaking syntax parsing.\n7. **Promotion:** Promote the updated generation skill to the global **Synapse Ledger** knowledge base.","metadata":{}}],"metadata":{"colab":{"from_bard":true},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}